ome visual representation of their  formless bodies perhaps as wrathful  angels descending upon him with flaming  swords  he saw nothing but the sound grew louder  unbearable  thundering and somehow it was worse  knowing they were there but being unable  to see them  face them try to appeal to them he spun  in dizzy circles  screaming apologies at the sky leaving  tiny malformed footprints in oni's blood  and still the spirits came like raging  harpies pressing against his body  stealing the thin air around him and  finally with a mighty cry he broke free  and ran  ran as hard and as fast as he had ever  run in his life  his legs pumping against the ground for  a brief moment he thought he had outrun  them  for the sound of their voices became  like a distant hellish wind  but then he felt his feet slipping out  from beneath him losing their fragile  purchase in the snow  and then he was flying through the  spirit soaked air the cold and death  seeping fast into his lungs  the shock of the freezing water as he  plunged into the black stream was enough  to stop his heart momentarily  but as he sputtered and struggled he was  able to roll over onto his back  flapping his numbing arms to try to stay  afloat he was so tired  so filled with horror and all he could  think of doing was floating all the way  back down to his own village in the arms  of the life-giving river  going back to his home and forgetting he  had ever seen oni  ever seen her haunted village tucked  among the high peaks  as he put his head back and considered  the cloud-choked sky above the bowl of  the mountaintops  he thought he might be able to do just  that forget  and then the spirits were upon him  shrieking down from above  and with their insubstantial weight they  pushed him beneath the freezing waves  holding them there with nothing but  their seething vengeance and the  tattered remnants of their unquiet souls  manny had a fleeting vision of his  stunted body floating in the lake near  his village  a felon coming to the lakeside with her  big iron pot  both of them would be there together in  the very center of the palm of the god's  hand  and then the water filled his lungs and  all was soothing darkness  you
 

